{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1177696-roleplaying-fugue","id":1177696,"title":"Roleplaying fugue","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-20T15:21:33-08:00","id":1177696,"title":"Roleplaying fugue","content":"So my NWO agent has fugue as a derangement. Is their having fugue anything like the movie Memento and the constant state of &quot;now&quot; that Attention Deficit Disorder - primarily Inattention Type causes? Can anyone recommend stuff to read or watch that would help? How have you ST'd or played fugue?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T06:12:34-08:00","id":1177826,"title":"","content":"Fugue states refer to a real form of psychosis where one's consciousness dissociates from reality for a period of time. Depending on a number of circumstances, it could be for minutes, days, and in some cases years.<br /> <br /> When one is in a fugue state, they might be anything from catatonic to completely active. It's not until after they exit the state that they become aware of the world around them. They might find themselves in a different country, a different set of clothes, or even in the middle of a conversation with someone they've never met before. Causes are varied, but they tend to come out of high stress situation. Fugue states are thought to be a coping mechanism for the consciousness if put in a situation it just can't handle. It's not too dissimilar to DID (Dissociative Identity Disorder, akak Multiple Personality Disorder) But instead of having another consciousness &quot;Take over&quot;, someone in a fugue state may be on auto pilot, or living as though within a dream.<br /> <br /> Memento isn't a bad example of how it feels to wake up from a fugue state, but it's not the same thing, since someone who came out of a fugue state is still capable of forming new memories, they just can't for the life of them piece together the events that led up to this moment. It's as though a period of their life just fell away from them.<br /> <br /> If one of my players were fugue, then I would have a lot of fun with their character any time the player couldn't make a session. The other players might witness them doing things or randomly dissapearing. And when the player returns they will have no idea where their character went, or what they did. Your agent, for example, might start of a session looking at the white house with a gun in their hand with no explanation beyond that. Or I might make them &quot;wake up&quot; in the middle of a poker game with some particularly unsavoury characters. Whatever serves the story best and makes things interesting for the player.<br /> <br /> As for playing a fugue state character, I'd say talk to your story teller and make sure they're on board with the idea that they will mostly be in control of how it plays out. You'd have to be a particularly strong RPer to do it all on your own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T14:41:18-08:00","id":1185354,"title":"","content":"Right now, my PC divides their time between the local freehold and the local Construct, so this will get interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}